OL,3,AWe have a duty to 'progress' Good
OL,4,AFriday Agreement, taoiseach tells PM
OL,5,
OL,6,FTaoiseach (Irish prime minister)
OL,7,FMicheal Martin has told Prime Minister
OL,8,FAndy Burnham their governments have a
OL,9,Fduty to "mind and progress" the 1998
OL,10,FGood Friday Agreement.
OL,12,FBurnham said the relationship between
OL,13,Fthe UK and Ireland matters "on every
OL,14,Fsingle level" as they met at Number 10
OL,15,FNorth for talks on Friday.
OL,17,FThe pair were expected to discuss a
OL,18,Ffurther strengthening of ties including
OL,19,Fboosting trade, security and working
OL,20,Fwith the European Union.
OL,23,APub: 18-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
